---
import ArcadeShell from '../../components/games/ArcadeShell.astro';
import ProofreaderLogo from '../../components/games/ProofreaderLogo.astro';
import '../../styles/proofreader.css';
---

<ArcadeShell
  game="proofreader"
  title="Proofreader"
  lead="Enter a genome-maintenance simulation: explore layered biotech laboratories, work around cover, and bring three distinct tools to six handcrafted missions."
  controls="WASD moves · mouse/drag aims · click/F fires · Space jumps · Shift sprints · R reloads · E interacts · 1–3 selects tools · P pauses. Touch: left moves, right aims; use Fire, Jump, and the tool buttons."
>
  <ProofreaderLogo slot="logo" size={42} />
  <Fragment slot="hud">
    <div class="arcade-stat"><span>Integrity</span><strong data-proof-health>100</strong></div>
    <div class="arcade-stat"><span>Ammunition</span><strong data-proof-ammo>24 / 120</strong></div>
    <div class="arcade-stat"><span>Floor</span><strong data-proof-floor>1 / 2</strong></div>
    <div class="arcade-stat"><span>Score</span><strong data-proof-score>0</strong></div>
    <div class="arcade-stat"><span>Best</span><strong data-proof-best>0</strong></div>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="playfield">
    <div class="proof-mission-display" aria-hidden="true">
      <span data-proof-bearing>↑</span><div>
        <strong data-proof-objective>Explore the atrium</strong><small data-proof-distance></small>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-reticle" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    <div class="proof-hit-marker" aria-hidden="true">×</div>
    <div class="proof-damage-edge" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="proof-weapon-readout" aria-hidden="true">
      <span data-proof-weapon>Precision carbine</span><small data-proof-reload></small>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-context" data-proof-context></div>
    <div class="proof-boss" data-proof-boss hidden>
      <span></span><progress max="180" value="180" aria-label="Guardian phase integrity"></progress>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-map" data-proof-map-panel hidden>
      <canvas
        width="360"
        height="400"
        data-proof-map
        aria-label="Sector map. Your position is a teal arrow; the objective is a gold dot."
      ></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-stick" data-proof-stick hidden aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
    <div class="proof-touch-actions">
      <button type="button" data-proof-sprint aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Hold to sprint"
        >Sprint</button
      >
      <button type="button" data-proof-jump aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Jump">Jump</button>
      <button
        type="button"
        data-proof-fire
        aria-pressed="false"
        class="proof-fire"
        aria-label="Fire selected weapon; drag on touch to aim while firing">Fire</button
      >
    </div>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="actions">
    <div class="proof-arsenal" aria-label="Weapon selection">
      <button type="button" data-proof-weapon="carbine" aria-pressed="true"
        ><small>01</small> Carbine</button
      >
      <button type="button" data-proof-weapon="scatter" aria-pressed="false"
        ><small>02</small> Scatter</button
      >
      <button type="button" data-proof-weapon="pulse" aria-pressed="false"
        ><small>03</small> Pulse</button
      >
    </div>
    <div class="proof-tools">
      <button type="button" data-proof-reload>Reload</button>
      <button type="button" data-proof-use disabled>Use</button>
      <button type="button" data-proof-cycle>Next tool</button>
      <button type="button" data-proof-lock>Lock mouse</button>
      <button type="button" data-proof-map-toggle>Map · M</button>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
  <div slot="readout" class="arcade-ribbon proof-log">
    <strong>Mission log</strong><span data-proof-notice
      >Choose a sector or begin your expedition.</span
    ><small data-proof-checkpoint>Mission entry</small>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="guide">
    <div class="proof-guide-grid">
      <section>
        <h3>Explore in three dimensions</h3><p>
          Ramps and stairs connect every required destination. Bridges have real space below them.
          Look up for drones and raised firing positions. The compass points toward the next
          objective; ↑ and ↓ beside its distance indicate another floor. M opens a floor-aware map.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Choose your tool</h3><p>
          <strong>Carbine:</strong> precise, sustained medium-range fire. <strong>Scatter:</strong> a
          close-range burst that rewards careful positioning. <strong>Pulse:</strong> a slower explosive
          projectile for groups. All three are available immediately. Each has its own magazine and reserve
          ammunition; R reloads.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Read the encounter</h3><p>
          Scouts reposition; horned chargers commit to a rush after a warning; armored sentries
          protect their front; winged drones move above the floor. Gold rings announce attacks.
          Walls, bridges, and machinery block fire. Vents and barriers show a steady amber warning
          before becoming harmful.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Recover and continue</h3><p>
          Use blue ammunition consoles with E, or the Use button, for free refills. Break marked
          crates for supplies. Safe-sector checkpoints restore integrity and ammunition after an
          encounter. Defeat offers a checkpoint retry; Restart always begins the entire mission.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Master the campaign</h3><p>
          Uninterrupted clears can earn three medals: clear, at least 70% shot accuracy, and no
          damage. A scatter volley or pulse explosion counts as one accurate shot if it damages an
          enemy. Checkpoint clears unlock the next mission but are unranked. Practice has unlimited
          shots and prevents damage without saving progress.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Play comfortably</h3><p>
          Mouse lock is optional: drag to aim if it is unavailable. On phones, the left thumb moves
          and the right side aims; drag the Fire button to aim while firing. Push the movement stick
          fully forward to sprint. Landscape Focus view gives the largest playfield. Graphics, field
          of view, motion, aiming assistance, and key bindings are adjustable below.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <h3>The biological inspiration</h3>
    <p>
      This is a fictional genome-maintenance simulation, not a molecular model. Its robotic threats
      and energy tools do not represent literal DNA repair, and genetic variation is not inherently
      harmful.
    </p>
    <p>
      In bacterial DNA polymerase III, the ε subunit can remove a mispaired terminal nucleotide
      using 3′→5′ exonuclease activity, while α resumes synthesis in the 5′→3′ direction. For
      example, a template 3′ A G C 5′ pairs with nascent DNA 5′ T C G 3′ after an incorrect terminal
      base is removed and replaced. This differs from correcting established substitutions or indels
      elsewhere in a genome.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a
        href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC392229/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Original study of Pol III proofreading</a>
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ArcadeShell>
<script>
  import { initProofreader, type ProofreaderController } from '../../scripts/proofreader';
  let controller: ProofreaderController | null = null;
  const mount = () => {
    controller ??= initProofreader(document);
  };
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', mount);
  document.addEventListener('astro:before-swap', () => {
    controller?.destroy();
    controller = null;
  });
  mount();
</script>
